2. **The 101,873 distantly supervised documents function as de facto training data.** The paper claims "no human annotations" and "no training," but selecting and conditioning on 100K+ labeled documents is functionally equivalent to training. An analysis of how performance scales with the size of 𝒟^dist (e.g., 1K, 10K, 50K, 100K) would reveal whether the framework actually relies on massive supervision under a different name.

